 Check PR-pending entities using the same logic as the startup hook: a terminal row carrying a valid merged sentinel (`pr-merge:` or `local-merge:`) bypasses `gh` and resumes `merge guard` directly, while bare PR rows (including terminal rows still carrying `mod-block: merge:pr-merge`) run `gh pr view` and advance through the same committed sentinel then guard path. This is the workflow's PR-pending scan: the generic event loop fires this idle hook and owns no PR scan of its own, so a workflow with no `pr-merge` mod never reaches for `gh` in its loop. Report any advanced entities to the captain.
 
+## Explicit knowledge delivery
+
+Knowledge output uses `spacedock merge guard {slug} --workflow-dir {dir} --delivery knowledge --verdict passed`. It requires an approved terminal Briefing whose single committed Markdown artifact contains one declaration:
+
+````markdown
+```spacedock-knowledge-delivery
+{"type":"KnowledgeDelivery","version":"1","outcome":"change","product":{"root":"main","base":"FULL_TRUNK_COMMIT","head":"FULL_HEAD_COMMIT"},"evidence":[{"uri":"git-root://state/FULL_COMMIT/evidence.md","rev":"sha256:RAW_FILE_DIGEST"}]}
+```
+````
+
+The native locked consumer checks the exact selected attempt and Briefing digest, resolves the immutable declaration and evidence, rejects every PR/merge claim, and checks an empty product diff against the configured local trunk. Product HEAD must match the declaration and the checkout must be clean. Product and state must be separate Git roots; use `root: worktree` with the exact `product.worktree` path when the entity records a repository-relative worktree, otherwise `root: main`. Missing objects or evidence refuse without consuming approval. Plain prose, an arbitrary hash, and the flag alone supply no authority.
+
+The knowledge write checks the entire entity snapshot and clears its mod-block with approval consumption. Repeating that consumed delivery validates the original approval, frozen evidence, terminal PASSED state and completed stamp without spending again. Existing product sentinels keep their existing meaning; never invent `local-merge:{reason}` or mark accepted knowledge rejected.
+
+The command must report `signal: finalized` before cleanup; exit zero alone is insufficient. An archive refusal is not completion: retain the task and evidence until the native archive guard accepts the consumed knowledge proof; do not force archive or fabricate delivery. Existing approvals without the declaration require explicit native rebinding by their owner, preserving prior authority as history. Exercise the consumer/refusal contract with `go test ./internal/gates -run TestKnowledge` and the complete journey with `go test ./internal/status -run TestKnowledgeMergeNativeArchive`.
+
 ## Hook: merge
 
 Resolve the PR base once: `BASE=$(spacedock dispatch trunk --workflow-dir {dir})` — the workflow's configured integration trunk (default `main` when no `trunk:` key is set). `dispatch trunk` emits exactly a **bare branch name** (e.g. `main`), so `$( )` yields `$BASE` clean (command substitution strips the single trailing newline). Retain the workflow-supplied `{branch}` as the data value `BRANCH`. Always quote `"$BASE"` and `"$BRANCH"` at use sites; do not evaluate either as shell syntax.
